THE OFFLINE FLOOR -- the same 351 lines through the fixed grammar
(`Playthrough::Mechanics` with `model: false`), no model, no key, no spend. This is
what a classifier call is bought against, and it is free.

  right                    0.427
    resolved          76   the grammar produced an answer the label accepts
    refused           74   the grammar refused, and the label says the line earns a refusal
    wrong              9   the grammar produced an answer the label does not accept -- silently
    over_refused     179   the grammar refused a line the label says should have played
    unparsed          13   no verb it knows and no exit by that name, so the whole grammar is printed

  `refused` is GENEROUS to the grammar: it counts a refusal on a line the label
  says earns one, and the grammar has no refusal KINDS to check -- its refusals are
  strings it composes, not `Playthrough::Refusal` objects. So the floor can say
  whether a line was refused and never which kind. It has no `also_named` at all.

